nds":"2026-10-24T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.b7706cb96d83e86d90f0fd7cf1c8f6d13428213c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 10:44PM MDT until October 24 at 12:15PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues along the\nRio Grande river and downstream waterways.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Mineral County and Rio Grande County...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1215 PM MDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will continue along the Rio Grande from above\nSouth Fork to Monte Vista through Saturday morning.  Several roads\nremain closed and housing areas evaacuated due to high water. While\nthe upper reaches of the Rio Grande from South Fork to Del Norte\nshould see steadily decreasing water levels, river levels will\ncontinue to rise between Del Norte to Monte Vista as the runoff\nflows downstream.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1032 PM MDT, local law enforcement reported flooding in the\nwarned area. Flooding is already occurring.\n- Highway 160 remains closed between South Fork and Wolf Creek\npass.  Please heed all road closuers.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMonte Vista, Del Norte and South Fork.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-24T12:15:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6ed6bf45cfd2c9b7e2914c85b381b2ff9ad5afc7.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-24T11:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 241129 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 529 AM MDT Sat Oct 24 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Focus for heavier rainfall shifts to the eastern plains today and Sunday. -